  "question": {
    "text": "Some ideal monoatomic gas <math> <mtext>A</mtext> </math> in an enclosure has a pressure <math><mtext>P</mtext></math> and the temperature <math> <mrow> <mtext>T</mtext></mrow></math>. Another ideal monoatomic gas <math> <mtext>B</mtext> </math> enclosed in a container of the same volume has a pressure <math><mn>2</mn><mtext>P</mtext></math> and the temperature <math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mtext>T</mtext> <mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></math>. The ratio of the average kinetic energy per molecule of gas <math> <mtext>A</mtext> </math> to gas <math> <mtext>B</mtext> </math> is"
